# Tests

Detect the runner from `composer.json` (`pestphp/pest` vs `phpunit/phpunit`). Do not convert Pest ↔ PHPUnit. Do not delete tests without approval.

**Do:** feature tests for HTTP/behavior; factories already in `database/factories`; assert authorization and validation failures; run the narrowest `php artisan test --filter=` that covers the change.

**Don't:** call real third-party APIs; require production secrets; mock the class under test into meaninglessness; rewrite passing tests to match a style guide.

```php
// Don't — hits a live provider
Http::get('https://api.stripe.com/v1/charges');

// Do — isolate outbound HTTP the way sibling tests already do
Http::fake();
```

Prefer extending an existing test file over a new suite. Boost `testing-best-practices` (if installed in the app) owns Pest/PHPUnit syntax; this rule only constrains project safety.
